          "source_quote": "καὶ μήτιγε",
          "english_quote": "And surely",
          "issue": "The particle admits materially different tentative and scalar forces: a cautious suggestion such as “perhaps,” or an emphatic transition such as “not to mention.” The draft selects emphatic assurance without explaining that choice or preserving the tentative alternative. The confirmed printed punctuation does not by itself settle the particle’s force.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining the contextual basis for the emphatic rendering and preserving the tentative alternative. Explicitly compare “And surely” with “And perhaps” and “Not to mention that.” If the tentative reading is selected, revise the opening accordingly and submit the revised wording for fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "διαβάλλων δὲ διδασκάλους ἀληθείας εἰς ἐνέδραν τῶν ἀκρίτων",
          "english_quote": "But because he slanders teachers of truth as a snare for the undiscerning",
          "issue": "The main rendering defensibly treats the undiscerning as the targets of the snare, but the genitive τῶν ἀκρίτων can also identify those responsible for the ambush into which the teachers are led. That alternative changes the participants’ roles and is not disclosed in the note on διάβολος.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a note explaining why the objective reading, “to ensnare the undiscerning,” is preferred, while preserving the subjective alternative, “into an ambush laid by the undiscerning against the teachers.” This requires disclosure, not automatic replacement of the defensible main rendering.",
